      "message": "It looks like this boolean is simply a cache of LockdownVpnTracker.isEnabled(). For this change I suggest adding a comment to that effect.\n\nWould it be reasonable in a future change to remove this boolean completely and call that method whenever needed ? It would simplify the locking logic. If that\u0027s not realistic and we do need a cache, we could have a method called isLockdownEnabled returning mLockdownTracker !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 mLockdownTracker.isEnabled(), and then move the cache to the lockdown tracker which I believe would be a bit easier to reason about than to make sure these two members are always kept in sync.\nIf you think this suggestion has merit then maybe we can add a TODO for now.",
